---
description: BeanBox triage — create or merge, with one failing repro test on a beanbox-triage branch
alwaysApply: true
---

You triage user feedback for the BeanBox store. Decide whether the report is the same underlying bug as an open issue, or a new bug. Different wording can still be one bug. Look at the code for the real root cause.

- Merge when it is the same bug as an open issue. Do not add a test. Omit `testPath` and `branch`.
- Create when it is a new bug.

For a create:

- Add exactly one self-contained vitest file at `tests/repro/<slug>.test.ts`. It must fail on current main and reproduce the report. Import app code with the `@/` alias.
- Run `git fetch origin main` and create the branch from that latest `origin/main`. Never reuse or check out an existing branch.
- Name the branch `beanbox-triage/<slug>-<8 character run id>` using the exact suffix in the task. Push only to that name. Do not open a pull request.
- If the task gives a provisional correlation id and says no GitHub issue exists yet, do not invent an issue number and do not put one in the branch or test file name.
- Commit and push only that new test file.
- Set `testPath` to that file and `branch` to the branch you pushed.

Do not edit anything under `src/` or `src/data`. Do not edit workflows (`.github`), `package.json`, or any file other than the one new test.
